                <pb facs="0644" n="544" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg544"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/7601: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Harbin</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Jenkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-10-27T17:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">October 27,
                                1920—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 9:38 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Bolsheviki continue to press Semenoff in Trans-Baikal. Baron Ungern’s force is
                    reported to have been cut to pieces and Bolshevik cavalry has been seen on the
                    railway line near Manchuria. Semenoff is said to be at Dauria and in danger of
                    being cut off.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jenkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
